vLLM 0.34 turns on the extensible KV cache by default on CUDA: it reserves the pool's address range, commits
physical pages as warmup needs them, and sizes the pool after warmup and CUDA-graph capture. KVarN's batched flush
writes int4 tiles into the pool from the metadata builder, outside the model's forward, and a warmup step's dummy
blocks lie past what the cache has committed by then. So every KVarN profile without a --kv-cache-memory pin
(SPEC=off CTX=huge, SPEC=mtp CTX=huge, batch KV=kvarn) died in capture with an illegal memory access in
_batched_flush (boots of every documented launcher default on an RTX 3090, 11-19).

The flush now commits what it writes first, as upstream's own warmups do with ensure_kv_cache_blocks. A KVarN block
id is a kernel block (one tile), several to a cache block, so the cache block each write needs comes from its
address: ExtensibleKVCache.blocks_backing(end_ptr). Before sizing, kv_blocks_writable commits up to the highest; once
the cache is sized it commits nothing, and a write past the committed count (only a warmup leftover, since the
scheduler never hands those blocks out) is dropped while the caller still frees its slot. Without an extensible
cache both helpers return None and nothing changes.

Measured with the cache on, against the same profiles with it off (an RTX 3090, the 0.34 image with
these files laid over it): all three profiles boot and print the cache-off texts; the 128-residue sweep on
SPEC=mtp CTX=huge PREFIX_CACHE=1 has 0 broken, with the same answer as cache off; a DEBUG boot logs no commit after
the extension, and warmup peaks at 105 of 206 blocks. The pool is 6.9-13.5% smaller than with the cache off. That
is the cache's own sizing margin, the same as on the non-KVarN profiles.

An earlier version committed max(tile id) + 1 as if it were a block count. It over-committed: the whole reservation
in warmup (the cache then shrank to fit), and up to capacity again after the first long request, 0.52 GiB past the
measured budget on the 3090 and 1.9 GiB on a 4090. Answers stayed right.

This replaces the opt-out it was folded into, which turned the extensible cache off for KVarN cache dtypes.

Kind: own
What: KVarN's batched flush commits the extensible KV cache's blocks it writes (found from the write's address), so
  unpinned KVarN profiles boot on 0.34 with the cache on; the KVarN half is in `kvarn/files`
Upstream: none
Cut-against: 0.34.0
Retires-when: rides with KVarN

